---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Support Amido';
const description =
  'Get help with Amido, report a bug, or share feedback about the AI food logger for people with type 1 diabetes.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
          <img src="/tippy-icon.png" alt="Amido" class="w-20 h-20 rounded-2xl mx-auto mb-6 shadow-md" />
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 tracking-tight">
            Support Amido
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
            Questions, bug reports and feedback are all welcome — and they make Amido better.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-16">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">An independent project</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Amido is an <strong class="text-gray-900">independent project</strong> built by a
            single developer, for people living with type 1 diabetes who want carbohydrate
            counting to be less of a chore — by describing a meal in plain words, or scanning a
            photo or barcode.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            There is no advertising and no data selling here. Your diary is stored on your
            device, not on our servers, and there is no cross-device sync. You can export a
            backup file in Settings → Your data, import it on another device, and delete the
            on-device diary at any time. Amido has no diabetes-specific integration.
          </p>
        </div>


        <div class="mb-16">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 text-center">Common questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <details class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900">Is Amido paid?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Yes. Amido is available as a monthly subscription (Amido Pro) purchased in the
                App Store or on Google Play. The subscription includes the AI meal analysis,
                photo and barcode logging, and the device-local diary with export and restore.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900">How do I manage or cancel my subscription?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Manage or cancel it in the store where you subscribed: App Store → Account →
                Subscriptions on iPhone, or Google Play → Payments &amp; subscriptions on Android.
                Cancelling stops the next renewal; access continues until the paid period ends.
                On the web, use the link in the Stripe receipt or contact support.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900">Where is my diary stored?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                On your device. Meals, ingredients, quantities and nutrition values are kept in
                the app's local database and are not uploaded to our servers. The account is used
                for the AI service, fair-use limits and subscriptions.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900">How do I back it up?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Open Settings → Your data → Export backup. The app creates a JSON file and opens
                the system share sheet, so you can save it to iCloud Drive, Google Drive, Files or
                anywhere else. Import it later from the same screen.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900">Does my diary sync between devices?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                No. There is no cross-device sync. Export a backup on one device and import it on
                the other. This keeps the diary out of our servers, but it also means the file is
                the only way to move it.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900">Is it included in iCloud or Google backup?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                If device backup is enabled, the operating system may include the diary in its
                backup. That copy is controlled by Apple or Google and is not accessible to us.
                You can also export your own backup at any time.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900">What happens if I delete the app?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                The diary on the device is removed. You can restore it from an exported backup, or
                from an iCloud/Google device backup if one exists. Export a copy before
                uninstalling if you might want the data back.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900">How do I delete my data?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Settings → Your data → Delete diary removes the on-device entries. Deleting your
                account removes the account, usage counters and subscription data from our
                servers.
              </p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-16">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 text-center">Feedback &amp; bug reports</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-center mb-6">
            Found something wrong? Have an idea? I'd love to hear from you.
          </p>
          <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <a
              href="https://github.com/emavgl/tippy-website/issues"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="block group"
            >
              <div class="bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 hover:border-gray-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all h-full">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                  <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-gray-100 flex items-center justify-center group-hover:bg-gray-200 transition-colors">
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-700" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 8v4m0 4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
                    </svg>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 group-hover:text-gray-700 transition-colors">GitHub Issues</h3>
                    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Report bugs &amp; request features</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a href="mailto:emavgl.app@gmail.com" class="block group">
              <div class="bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 hover:border-gray-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all h-full">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                  <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-gray-100 flex items-center justify-center group-hover:bg-gray-200 transition-colors">
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-700" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" />
                    </svg>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 group-hover:text-gray-700 transition-colors">Email</h3>
                    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-0.5">emavgl.app@gmail.com</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4 text-center">
            Please don't include private health or account information in public GitHub issues.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-xl mx-auto">
            Thank you for using Amido.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-4">
            — <a href="https://github.com/emavgl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand hover:underline">emavgl</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
